$(
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
  Filter limits
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
$)

  $c FilMap $.
  $c fLimf $.

  $c fLim $.
  $c fClus $.
  $c fClusf $.

  $( Extend class definition to include the neighborhood filter mapping
     function. $)
  cfm $a class FilMap $.

  $( Extend class notation with a function returning the limit of a filter. $)
  cflim $a class fLim $.

  $( Extend class definition to include the function for filter-based function
     limits. $)
  cflf $a class fLimf $.

  $( Extend class definition to include the cluster point function on
     filters. $)
  cfcls $a class fClus $.

  $( Extend class definition to include the function for cluster points of a
     function. $)
  cfcf $a class fClusf $.

  ${
    $d f g j t x y $.
    $( Define a function that takes a filter to a neighborhood filter of the
       range.  (Since we now allow filter bases to have support smaller than
       the base set, the function has to come first to ensure that curryings
       are sets.)  (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 5-Sep-2009.)  (Revised by
       Stefan O'Rear, 20-Jul-2015.) $)
