         ( x filGen ran ( t e. y |-> ( f " t ) ) ) ) ) $.

    $( Define a function (indexed by a topology ` j ` ) whose value is the
       limits of a filter ` f ` .  (Contributed by Jeff Hankins,
       4-Sep-2009.) $)
    df-flim $a |- fLim = ( j e. Top , f e. U. ran Fil |->
     { x e. U. j | ( ( ( nei ` j ) ` { x } ) C_ f /\ f C_ ~P U. j ) } ) $.

    $( Define a function that gives the limits of a function ` f ` in the
       filter sense.  (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 14-Oct-2009.) $)
    df-flf $a |- fLimf = ( x e. Top , y e. U. ran Fil |->
        ( f e. ( U. x ^m U. y ) |-> ( x fLim ( ( U. x FilMap f ) ` y ) ) ) ) $.

    $( Define a function that takes a filter in a topology to its set of
       cluster points.  (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 10-Nov-2009.) $)
    df-fcls $a |- fClus = ( j e. Top , f e. U. ran Fil |->
      if ( U. j = U. f , |^|_ x e. f ( ( cls ` j ) ` x ) , (/) ) ) $.

    $( Define a function that gives the cluster points of a function.
       (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 24-Nov-2009.) $)
    df-fcf $a |- fClusf = ( j e. Top , f e. U. ran Fil |->
      ( g e. ( U. j ^m U. f ) |-> ( j fClus ( ( U. j FilMap g ) ` f ) ) ) ) $.
  $}

